 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? A sketch is quick drawing, often only one or two pages, done quickly for fun. A study, on the other hand, is a detailed, careful drawing of one object or scene. Sort of. Homework usually means a task set by a teacher, and it' usually about learning something, like a new technique. A huge challenge, and a great thing to practice with. Clouds are the hardest thing to get right. Would you rather do a study of one cloud, or draw several different clouds in the same image? Pick one thing to improve. Could it be the softness of the sky, or the shape of the clouds? Good choice. A few studies of the same cloud will teach you more than one drawing.",
